Let $A$ be a finite commutative ring of universe $u+1$, let $f:X	o Y$ be a morphism of schemes of universe $u$ [def-pc-scheme], and let $c=(X\xrightarrow{j}Z\xrightarrow{p}Y)$ be a compactification of $f$, so $j$ is open, $p$ proper and $p\circ j=f$ [def-weil-compactifications-refinements]. Use ordinary unbounded constant-$A$ module derived categories on the etale and pro-etale sites [def-weil-pbc-derived-categories] [def-weil-pbc-proetale-modules]. Let $
u_T^*$ denote the exact derived site comparison pullback [def-sf-comparison-derived-pullback], $F_c^{\mathrm{et}}=Rp_{\mathrm{et},*}Dj_!^{\mathrm{et}}$ the ordinary etale compact-support candidate [def-amb-etale-compact-support], and $F_c^{\mathrm{proet}}=Rp_{\mathrm{proet},*}Dj_!^{\mathrm{proet}}$ the corresponding unbounded pro-etale candidate using the actual extension by zero and derived direct image [def-weil-pbc-proetale-operations] [def-weil-extension-by-zero]. Define the natural isomorphism $F_c^{\mathrm{proet}}
u_X^*\iota\simeq
u_Y^*F_c^{\mathrm{et}}\iota$, where $\iota:D^+(X_{\mathrm{et}},A)	o D(X_{\mathrm{et}},A)$ is inclusion, as follows: first commute open extension by zero with site comparison; then use the inverse of the specified direct-image counit-mate isomorphism $
u_Y^*Rp_{\mathrm{et},*}\simeq Rp_{\mathrm{proet},*}
u_Z^*$, with its bounded-below compatibility identifications and the canonical functor associators. This is a fixed map in the ordinary categories on bounded-below etale inputs; no ambient exceptional right adjunction or special coefficient-field datum is part of this definition.
